Z||000004||Cheever2||04-05-2001||11:01 PM||||I kinda agree and sorta don't.<BR>First, people come here expecting it to be another car forum like all the others.  We know it isn't, but they don't.  And what are they accustomed to, at those others - the rat race.  My point being that they just don't know what a cool place this is, and that you just take your shoes off, sip on something soothing, and enjoy some enlightening discussion.<P>The flip side to that is, if they are already a part of the Fiero world, why didn't they come here <I>before</I> going to the other forums?  And if they are indeed new to Fieros, your point is dead on: they should hang out, read the posts and mingle for a while before expecting us to treat them as friends instead of the strangers they are.<P>Second, I don't see any harm when they have a variety of miscellaneous (thanks again Cliff for the spell checker) parts that are relatively inexpensive.  I myself took the risk recently of ordering something from such a member, and can now report and give either high or low marks.  The flip side of this one is: when you're talking about an entire car in decent running condition, or some high-dollar service, for sure we want to know who we're dealing with.  We want to check your reputation with the others.<P>Third, this is surely to be expected as the membership grows the way it has.  Who knows what other growing pains there will be.  But we're all still Fiero enthusiasts, and the more the merrier.  The only flip side to that I can think of is that it's probably a good thing for someone like you, Hoop, to put up a checkpoint and say "Wait a minute, we don't even know who you are".<P>I appreciate what you're saying, and partially agree, but you said it yourself, this is a free world.  Besides, I don't see the veterans here going anywhere else, so the camaraderie, the flavor, the atmosphere and the giving and taking of both ideas and car parts will remain as they have been in the past.  We just have some new faces, with more coming every hour it seems.  It will all work out; those who don't belong will move on, the rest will stay & have a good ol' time.<P>It took me some time to get these thoughts onto the keyboard... I'll run the spell check now and see what other replies you got while I was doing this.  Who's next on the soapbox?<P><BR>||||reg||2
