Z||000040||stimpy||04-11-2001||09:38 AM||||Well, back when I was a young'n, we didn't have any fancy ENIACs or Timex-Sinclairs, if we wanted a "forum", we just projected our thoughts onto the face of the sun, then we would stare into the sun until our eye sockets caught afire. Then we would run around with our onion banging against our crotches with our head on fire, saying "Oh look at me, I tried to read other peoples thoughts off the face of the sun, and now my eyesockets are on fire!" And ya know what? We LIKED it! Flibberty Gibbitt!<P>Coming soon to a theater near you. "Voytek's Run" After years of exterminating the "Oldtimers" with his mighty flamegun, Voytek realizes he is now nearing 1000 post and he too will become an Oldtimer marked for flaming. ||||reg||1
Z||000041||Voytek||04-11-2001||11:23 AM||||Stimpy - you never cease to amaze me with your childish replies - I'm sure there's a kids' forum somewhere and you'd sound like the smartest guy there.... but then again, maybe not.  Not only wasn't your reply original, it was almost a copy of bhooper's last reply (??!!)<BR>tgowens - please read my message carefully.  I don't recall saying my feelings were hurt - it takes a lot more than that - simply an opinion on the 'drive-by's' bashing (I thought opinions were allowed on this Forum).  I don't know if 40-some posts makes me a youngster (I assume it was intended to insult me), but 40 relevant posts are worth a lot more than 500+ garbage ones (not talking about anyone in particular).  And as far as some of you 'old timers' talking on the phone, then adoring each other and kissing each other's butts on the forum -what you do in the privacy of your own home / computer is your business.  The problem is that while you help each other, the best advice SOME of you have to a good question is 'Go do a search' (???????!!!) (then again, there are some really helpful old-timers).<BR>Standard - threads about prostitutes and monkeys can be quite valuable, I'm sure.  What gets me is that the people participating in those threads have the nerve to gripe about the 'here-today,gone-tomorrow's'.<BR>I know some of you are boiling over and ready to explode right about now - keep your depends handy!||||reg||1
