Z||000044||Chris McDonald||04-11-2001||12:33 PM||||Whoa!<P>This is so funny.  I became involved in the Forum by selling my car.  In fact, my first post here was to sell the car.  Since then, I have really enjoyed sharing and gathering ideas from all of you.  <P>I sure am glad I did not see a post like this first.  I might not have ever joined the family.  <P>Darn, I can't think of anything else to really gripe about now either.  <P>Hope your day gets better.  Don't let all those new guys freak you out.  You never know, you might just buy something from one of them some day.  <P>Spell checker is way cool!  I will just have to remember to use it.||||reg||6
Z||000045||Tigger||04-11-2001||12:45 PM||||Voytek, sorry you have a gripe about technical questions not being answered as swiftly and promptly as you'd like.<P>I would like to think everyone here tries to help others with topics they are most familar with and can answer.  You have to understand, not everyone here is a certified SAE mechanic just sitting around waiting for you to ask a question.<P>Most questions that come up have been answered many times before.  Usually if you see someone with 5-10 posts asking a question like "My headlights don't go up."  You'll likely hear someone say "Do a search", to kindly tell them were to look for answers.  It saves us the time having to repeatedly answer the same question over and over so we can move on to answer other uncommon questions being asked or just joke around a bit like we are here.<P>The search function really does work.  If you return to the thread a short time later, most of the the time you'll see a response like "Ohh.. I found what I was looking for and I found the problem was...  Thanks!"     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  If the search doesn't work, a quick reply saying "I tried a few things, still having problems."  Then usually someone will jump in to offer suggestions or just happens to have had the same problem a week before.  If your technical question happens to go down in the pile of questions and you're not satisfied, just give it a <B><I>bump</I></B> to bring it back to the top.<P>light'en up Dude!<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 04-11-2001).]||||reg||1
