Z||000051||Voytek||04-12-2001||10:31 AM||||At the risk of becoming unpopular (yeah, what are the odds of that?) and sending this not-long-enough topic back to the top, here it goes:<BR>Tigger-man - thanks for that very thorough description of how to use the Search function.  Now whenever someone wants to do a Search, they can do a Search on it first!  How convenient is THAT?!<BR>Stimpy - finally a shorter and SOMEWHAT more original (and let's not forget less tacky) reply.  A good sense of humour ain't 'cheap' (pun) - let me know when you collect enough dough - I'll give you an address you can send it to.<BR>Oh, one more to Tigger - just in case you didn't notice, this topic had nothing to do with the promptness of answering tech. questions.  That was a thread that, at least as far as I remember, ended some time in March.  You can send it back to the top if you really want to.  Being one of the 'old timers' you stand a very good chance of getting a pat on the back (or a kiss on the rear) for bringing that back (really, no sarcasm intended).||||reg||1
Z||000052||stimpy||04-12-2001||12:44 PM||||While I realize a good sense of humor is priceless, I do feel that ANY degree of humor will be an apparent improvement over your steroid-induced surliness. For God's sake, man, watch cartoons and eat Fruit Loops once in your life.  Hang out with a girl who wears a stupid hat and funny sunlasses. Honk and wave at people you don't know and savor their confusion as they try to place you. The world can be a fun place, if you invest a bit in, you will definately cash in on it's dividends.<P>Peace & lighten up||||reg||1
