Z||000054||Tigger||04-12-2001||01:29 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B>Tigger-man - thanks for that very thorough description of how to use the Search function.  Now whenever someone wants to do a Search, they can do a Search on it first!  How convenient is THAT?!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey, your welcome, anytime.  I find the search very convenient, I've found the answers to many of my questions using it.  For example, not long ago I wanted to know the thread size of my manual shift knob.  To be honest, I searched and found nothing so I posted the question.  Guess what, it took a day or so before someone who knew the answer and posted.  (Thanks, danny boy & FieroJoe *gives them both a pat on the back*   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P>If someone tells you to do a search,(from an old timer or not) don't take it as an insult.  That is my point.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B>Tigger - just in case you didn't notice, this topic had nothing to do with the promptness of answering tech. questions.  That was a thread that, at least as far as I remember, ended some time in March.  You can send it back to the top if you really want to.  Being one of the 'old timers' you stand a very good chance of getting a pat on the back (or a kiss on the rear) for bringing that back (really, no sarcasm intended).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No, really I don't want to bring that thread back, just could tell your gripe was about other forum members wasting their time and yours.  I wouldn't want to waste any more of your time (sarcasm intended   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ).<P>Anyhoo, "Hey stimpy, can I give you a pat on the back, can I... huh? huh?" j/k<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 04-12-2001).]||||reg||1
