Z||000060||FieroBUZZ||05-12-2001||09:17 AM||||Just a small note from an outsider. I read the Forum for months before joining and posting anything.  Not everyone wants to jump in and be part of the crowd. <P> I do however, think it's not wrong for the newbies to jump in and try to sell something.  The regulars know if it's a rip-off and advise accordingly.  Who knows, you may come accross that part you need.  The guy selling a car may have another that he needs stuff for. <P>The strange posts (or replies) only add to the flavour IMHO. Some of the guys come across pretty strong, so what?  If you don't like a post, ignore it.  If you feel the need to answer don't get your knickers in a knot if someone else attacks.<P>If everyone thought the same way we would just have one post. "I love my Fiero" and 2300 answers.<P>Remember, if you close your eyes it will all go away and you'll be back in lala land.<P>Group Hug time...<P><BR>Oh, and one more thing...<P>All your base are belong to us!!!<P>Sorry...Gary||||reg||12
