Z||000067||Spektyr||05-13-2001||02:34 PM||||It figures the Hookers would be with the muffler bearings... exhaust parts.<P>I'm sure there's a HEADer joke in there somewhere, but I don't think I'll look for it.  I'd probably get arrested (or flamed).<P>BTW, I think Stimpy and I might've done time in one of those 'white jacket with long sleeves' institutions together.  Ya know, the kind where they tie the sleeves behind your back as a pratical joke...<P>I think his off-topic remarks are very funny, and reflect a moderately warped psyche (just like mine!).  Remember kids, the difference between imagination and insanity is just a shade of grey.<P>Or put another way, the lunatic can tell the difference between reality and fantasy.  He just likes his fantasy better.  The truely insane person can't see reality anymore.  I can still pretend to be a 'normal' person, so I'm just a lunatic.<P><B>BIG DOGS!  JUMPING ON MY FACE!</B><P>Ahem.  But as was mentioned earlier, it's hard to drive a Fiero without a sense of humor (or a small intestine, for that matter).  I think the Fiero comes in fourth in jokes, right behind Blondes, Lawyers, and Pollocks.  That just makes it all the more satisfying when you blow the doors off someone.<P>"D00d, U cant beet my phat r1cem0b1le!  Fiero's sux0r... heeeeey... you ain't supposed to be that fast!"<P>I may not be an 'oldtimer', but I will be.  I love to ask questions, and I especially love to post meaningless drivel on BS threads and generally kick back, crack open a cold one and let my mind run amok among friends.  I have more spare time than money to upgrade my Fiero, so it's fair to say I'll be hitting the 'magical' 1k mark before too long.<P>Um... do we get like a little gold pin or something for that by the way?  I get one at work when I hit 1 year.<P>Then again, maybe I am already an oldtimer... I used to program some MEAN basic...||||reg||1
